cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use batchdx-cyto, please cite this software *and* the upstream components that
  were actually enabled in your run. The run's resolved configuration and
  `docs/upstream_audit.md` record which those were; citing a component this build only
  declares, but could not execute, would misstate what produced your results.
title: "batchdx-cyto: batch-effect diagnosis, correction and evaluation for cytometry"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake-orchestrated system that diagnoses batch-associated differences in mass,
  conventional and spectral flow cytometry, assesses whether a technical interpretation
  is supported by the design, runs eligible correction methods independently against an
  identity baseline, and evaluates technical improvement separately from structural
  distortion.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mdmanurung/batchdx-cyto"
keywords:
  - cytometry
  - batch effect
  - CyTOF
  - spectral flow cytometry
  - reproducible workflows
authors:
  - name: "batchdx-cyto contributors"

